Film simulation model and data
------------------------------

    spektrafilm by Andrea Volpato
    https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm
    Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0

The physical film/paper model this crate implements is spektrafilm. Its
simulation code is GPL-v3; the profiles, spectral upsampling table, neutral
print-filter database and other data tables are CC BY-SA 4.0 under the terms in
licenses/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt (v1.1, 2026-05-28), which is shipped unmodified
and is also installed with the application under resources/licenses/x3f-render.

Every bundled data file is a byte-identical copy of the upstream file, so no
CHANGELOG.txt accompanies them:

  - assets/profiles/*.json      20 film and 8 paper profiles
  - assets/irradiance_xy_tc.npy spectral upsampling table
  - assets/neutral_print_filters.json  per-stock neutral enlarger filtration

Film and paper names identify the modeled materials and do not imply
affiliation or endorsement. "spektrafilm" is not used as X3Fuse branding.

Port source
-----------

spektrafilm-rs by turbasvin, GPL-3.0:
https://github.com/turbasvin/spektrafilm-rs
Pinned at v0.1.2, revision 9dd59b0. The WGSL kernels in src/render.wgsl and the
Rust parameter preparation in src/film/ are a direct port of that project's
`spektrafilm-shaders/wgsl`, `spektrafilm-core` and `spektrafilm-model` crates.
It is also used as an external parity oracle; see assets/PROVENANCE.md.

Spectral upsampling table
-------------------------

assets/irradiance_xy_tc.npy originates from Johannes Hanika's work for vkdt
(https://github.com/hanatos/vkdt, https://jo.dreggn.org/vkdt/) and is
distributed by spektrafilm under the CC BY-SA 4.0 terms above.

X3Fuse modifications to the code (not to the data)
--------------------------------------------------

  - Integration into this crate's single-device, single-submission, tiled pass
    list instead of spektrafilm-rs's whole-frame CPU round trips.
  - Spatial parameters are derived from the whole sensor frame at the current
    render scale, so cropping or requesting a region never changes a diffusion
    size or a grain particle.
  - Grain is anchored to native image coordinates rather than the tile-local
    pixel index, so tiles, regions and whole previews agree.
  - An added grain chroma control mixes the per-channel noise toward its
    achromatic mean.
  - `halation_midtones` gates the added halation by the blurred signal level;
    spektrafilm's separate highlight-boost stage is not ported.
  - The enlarger is normalised against an uncompensated mid-gray card
    (`normalize_print_exposure` without `print_exposure_compensation`).
    spektrafilm's default re-solves the print exposure at the compensated film
    exposure, which cancels a film exposure change back out and leaves only a
    shift in where the scene sits on the H&D curve; X3Fuse's film exposure
    control has to expose the film and let the print follow it.
  - Blurs whose radius would round away are skipped.
  - f32 preview precision throughout, against spektrafilm's f64 export path.
  - Stages not ported: glare, output gamut compression, highlight boost,
    unsharp (this crate has its own sharpening), the DIR coupler diffusion
    tail, camera/enlarger diffusion filters, camera and scanner lens blur, the
    mallett2019 and arctic2026alpha02 front passes, B&W development-time
    families, auto-exposure, the PCHIP 3D LUT export path, and the s023 print
    curve morph.

Runtime dependencies added for rendering/encoding include wgpu (MIT/Apache-2.0),
pollster (MIT/Apache-2.0), bytemuck (Zlib/Apache-2.0/MIT), serde/serde_json
(MIT/Apache-2.0), libm (MIT/Apache-2.0), half (MIT/Apache-2.0), and image
(MIT/Apache-2.0). image supplies PNG and genuine JPEG encoding; TIFF output uses
x3f-core's existing encoder. Their source and license terms remain available
through Cargo.lock and the associated crate distributions.
